 X("D-02","Security","Inventory.read warehouse and cost breadth","Inventory.read exposes stock quantities AND unit costs with no branch or warehouse filter, even though B6 site 3 now enforces warehouse scope exactly for CanUseWarehouseAsync. Read and warehouse-scope therefore disagree. Affected: every employee of an unconfigured company; every inventory role holder. Dimensions: Company (enforced), Branch (exists), Warehouse (enforced for use, not for read).","A) keep; B) warehouse/branch-scoped visibility; C) hide cost, show quantity; D) separate stock-cost permission","B plus D - warehouse/branch-scoped visibility AND a separate stock-cost permission. Cost is the sensitive field; quantity usually is not.","Read alignment with the enforced warehouse scope. Compatibility: buyers and clerks may lose cost visibility. Migration: seed scoped policy; introduce a cost permission code. Tests: extend the 8 Inventory focused tests. Screens: 78 Inventory views.","R6, R9","Owner","R6 entry","OPEN"),
 X("D-03","Security","CRM customer-data breadth","CrmAccessService.cs:59 returns TRUE for EVERY CRM action on a company with no configured roles - read, edit, and every other action. Exposed: all accounts, contacts, leads, opportunities, custom field values and bilingual fields. Affected: every authenticated employee of an unconfigured company. Dimensions: Company (enforced), Owner (see D-04), Team (OrgHierarchy exists), Branch.","A) mirror Accounting - read-only compatibility, all other actions Never; B) deny all; C) keep open; D) assigned/team/company policy explicitly selected","D, defaulting to A - require the policy to state assigned, team or company explicitly. The current behaviour is not a policy; it is the absence of one.","Unblocks CRM B6 site 1. Compatibility: unconfigured companies lose edit/delete. Migration: seed a CRM read policy per company. Tests: a CRM focused suite equivalent to the 14 Accounting tests. Screens: 32 Crm views.","R6, R11","Owner","R6 entry","OPEN"),
 X("D-04","Security","CRM unrestricted visible-owner scope","CrmAccessService.cs:98 returns NULL, and null means unrestricted - the widest possible answer, returned precisely when the system knows least. An unconfigured or misconfigured state currently maps SILENTLY to full visibility. Affected: every CRM list and search. Dimensions: Owner, Team via OrgHierarchy, Branch, Company.","A) own records only; B) team scope via OrgHierarchy; C) keep unrestricted; D) distinguish ConfigurationError from Unconfigured and fail closed on both","D then A - an unconfigured or error state must NEVER map silently to unrestricted null. Fail closed, then widen deliberately.","Unblocks CRM B6 site 2. Compatibility: users may lose visibility of records they do not own. Migration: an explicit scope decision per company. Tests: scope-exactness tests mirroring the 10 warehouse tests. Screens: all 32 Crm views.","R6, R11","Owner","R6 entry","OPEN"),
 # ---------------- APPROVED this increment
 X("D-32","Platform","Task Management ownership and boundary","Tasks already has a controller, 5 views, an access service, 7 SQL slices and 2 registered hosted services - it is not greenfield.","A) Tasks owns everything including its own timeline; B) split - Tasks owns state and rules, Communication owns collaboration; C) Communication absorbs Tasks","B - Tasks owns task entity, assignment, status, priority, due dates, dependencies, checklists, subtasks, escalation, time tracking and task-specific rules. Communication owns comments, mentions, attachments, reactions, followers, watchers, unified timeline rendering and notification generation contracts. Tasks PUBLISHES events to the shared timeline and must NOT maintain a second independent general timeline.","Prevents a second timeline implementation. Requires assessment of legacy task activity data before any migration. Work is integration and remediation, NOT greenfield task creation.","R5","Owner","Decided","APPROVED"),
 X("D-33","Platform","Calendar ownership and boundary","Calendar already has a service, controller and SQL slice - it is not greenfield.","A) Calendar owns all scheduling everywhere; B) Calendar owns calendar events and unified presentation only; C) each module owns its own calendar","B - Calendar Platform owns calendar events, recurrence, attendees, meeting metadata, availability, reminders, resource booking, schedule views and external calendar integration contracts. Tasks owns task due dates and task scheduling rules. Projects and Construction own their domain schedules, milestones and activities. Communication owns event comments, mentions and timeline entries. Calendar may DISPLAY tasks but is not their source of truth.","Calendar provides unified presentation and coordination, not ownership of all scheduling data. Requires assessment of the existing service, controller and schema before modification. Do not rebuild from zero.","R5","Owner","Decided","APPROVED"),
 X("D-35","Reporting","First production reporting dataset","No production module is bound as a live dataset. Business Events infrastructure and the Business Event Monitor already exist and are verified.","A) financial statements; B) stock valuation; C) sales analysis; D) Business Events / Platform Operations","D - the Business Events / Platform Operations dataset, READ-ONLY. Lower commercial sensitivity than Accounting, Inventory or CRM; proves the full pipeline (dataset layer, filters, parameters, catalog, HTML, CSV, Excel, history, archive, permissions, row caps) without exposing ledger balances, stock costs or customer data; delivers operational value immediately.","Pilot fields: EventId, EventType, EventVersion, EntityType, EntityId, CompanyId, BranchId where available, OccurredAt, ActorId, CorrelationId, consumer states, failure state, retry count, dispatch timing, non-sensitive operational metadata. Full sensitive payload is NOT exposed by default.","R4","Owner","Decided","APPROVED"),
 X("D-36","Platform","Canonical platform visual identity","crossbuy-brand.css currently overrides Metronic blue with ledger green and gold; CLAUDE.md records the contradiction as open.","A) green and gold; B) CrossBusiness Blue; C) selectable themes","B - CrossBusiness Blue is the canonical platform identity. Platform shell, Workspace, Report Studio, administration consoles, Construction workspace and Communication UI all use blue. Green and gold remain permitted INSIDE financial charts, accounting reports, profit and loss indicators and domain-specific data visualizations - but are not the default shell identity.","All new screens use blue. Existing production UI and crossbuy-brand.css are NOT modified in this increment. Implementation path is D-37.","R3","Owner","Decided","APPROVED"),
 X("D-38","Deployment","Canonical SQL deployment root","Two trees: deploy/sql (57 slices, plus the generated fresh/ build and the operational purge and backup scripts) and CrossBuy/deploy/sql (60 slices, plus manifest.json). The manifest GENERATOR and the schema-history reporter both live at CrossBuy/deploy/. deploy/README.md states the authoritative provisioning method is BACKUP/RESTORE of CrossBuyDB2, not script replay, because EF migrations are broken and ~90 ad-hoc scripts in C:/temp built the schema.","A) deploy/sql canonical; B) CrossBuy/deploy/sql canonical; C) keep both with a manifest; D) a new third root","B - CrossBuy/deploy/sql is the canonical AUTHORED-slice root, because the governance tooling (scan-sql-manifest.ps1, report-schema-history.ps1) and manifest.json already live beside it. deploy/ is retained and RE-LABELLED as the deployment PACKAGE root: generated artifacts (fresh/), operational scripts (backup, purge) and the server README - not an authoring root.","No file is moved or deleted in this increment. Migration of the 55 root-only module slices into the canonical root is an R1 action, executed slice by slice with hash verification.","R1","Owner","R1 entry","APPROVED - migration deferred to R1"),
 X("D-39","Deployment","Divergent same-name slice reconciliation","manifest.json already records 4 duplicateNames with identical=false and distinctHashes=2: pos_hold_recall, pos_order_guests, pos_quickmenu, pos_setup. It also flags 1 script as review (hm16_rename_grni.sql - unguarded, unread, DO NOT DEPLOY) and 1 as not-deployable (script.sql).","A) keep the newer by mtime; B) keep the canonical-root copy; C) diff and merge each pair deliberately; D) supersede both with a new reconciled slice","C then D - each pair is diffed and read by its owner, then superseded by ONE reconciled slice with a new SliceId. Choosing by mtime or by location would be guessing about schema.","Until reconciled, 'apply pos_setup.sql' is ambiguous - the manifest says so explicitly. The review and not-deployable scripts must be resolved or formally excluded before any environment promotion.","R1","Owner","R1 entry","APPROVED - direction"),
 X("D-40","Deployment","PlatformSchemaHistory canonical design","platform_schema_history.sql is authored but applied nowhere, so the table meant to answer 'which slices are applied here' cannot answer it. manifest.json answers the AUTHORED side (115 scripts with SHA-256 and apply rank) but has no database-side counterpart.","A) trust the manifest alone; B) database-side applied record keyed by SliceId + SHA-256; C) external deployment log","B - an applied record in each database: SliceId, filename, SHA-256, module, owner, dependencies, applied date, environment, result. The manifest is the authored registry; PlatformSchemaHistory is the applied registry. Neither replaces the other.","Enables drift detection: missing slice, changed applied slice, duplicate SliceId, same filename with a different hash, out-of-order dependency. Must be the FIRST slice applied in every environment.","R1","Owner","R1 entry","APPROVED - direction"),
 X("D-41","Product","CrossBusiness Workspace as the first integrated product","Three platforms have zero user reach; the product has no unified front door.","A) module-by-module UI improvement; B) a unified workspace as the first product; C) defer any UI until all platforms are activated","B - CrossBusiness Workspace is the first integrated user-facing product. It is NOT a new business module: it owns no Accounting, CRM, Task or Calendar data, orchestrates access through approved service contracts, must never bypass module permissions, uses CrossBusiness Blue, and requires an approved Metronic reference before UI implementation.","Defines R3. Workspace adds no permissions of its own - every read delegates to the owning module's access service.","R3","Owner","Decided","APPROVED"),
 X("D-12","Communication","Unified timeline ownership","Both the platform timeline projection and the Comm aggregator can render activity; Tasks could implement a third.","A) platform timeline canonical; B) Communication aggregator canonical; C) both with one canonical source","B for rendering, with business events as the canonical source of fact - Communication owns unified timeline rendering and notification generation contracts. Modules PUBLISH events; they do not build their own general timelines.","Resolved together with D-32. Tasks must not maintain a second independent general timeline.","R5","Owner","Decided","APPROVED"),
 # ---------------- Approved architecture DIRECTION (not production activation)
 X("D-05","Communication","Privacy ceiling","No maximum visibility is defined for comm content on any entity.","A) global internal-only ceiling; B) per-entity declared ceiling; C) per-thread choice","B - each entity registration DECLARES its maximum visibility. Employee: maximum Internal. Journal Entry: maximum Internal. Invoice: maximum Internal unless an external portal policy exists. Support Ticket: Internal or CustomerVisible by comment type. Public: only for explicitly approved external entities.","Gates Communication activation. Approved as architecture direction; production activation still requires R2.","R2","Owner","R2 entry","APPROVED - architecture direction"),
 X("D-06","Communication","Retention policy","No retention is defined for threads, notifications, attachments or audit.","A) indefinite; B) per-entity declared retention; C) one global period","B - each entity registration declares retention duration, archive behaviour, legal-hold behaviour, deletion/anonymization behaviour and attachment retention.","Gates activation and audit. Approved as architecture direction.","R2","Owner","R2 entry","APPROVED - architecture direction"),
 X("D-07","Communication","Per-entity audit policy","CommAuditWriter exists but per-entity policy is undefined.","A) audit everything; B) audit sensitive entities; C) per-entity declaration","C - each entity registration declares edit-history, deletion-history, read-receipt, attachment-audit and immutable-history requirements.","Gates the DocComments migration. Approved as architecture direction.","R2","Owner","R2 entry","APPROVED - architecture direction"),
 X("D-13","Communication","Support external-principal model","No model exists for a customer participating in a thread; a customer is currently representable only as an employee BusinessContext, which would be wrong.","A) no external participation; B) mirrored portal identity; C) a distinct ExternalPrincipalContext","C - a customer must NOT be treated as an employee BusinessContext. Requires a future ExternalPrincipalContext ADR before any implementation.","Support must NOT be activated until this exists. Approved as architecture direction only.","R11","Owner","R11 entry","APPROVED - architecture direction, ADR required"),
 X("D-14","Communication","Customer-visible comments","No distinction exists between internal notes and customer-facing replies.","A) never customer-visible; B) explicit per comment; C) per thread","B - two explicit comment types: InternalNote and CustomerVisibleReply. Explicit and auditable per comment.","Gates portal support. Approved as architecture direction.","R11","Owner","R11 entry","APPROVED - architecture direction"),
 X("D-15","Communication","@Role reverse membership resolution","Mention by role requires reverse role-to-user resolution, which no component owns.","A) platform role directory; B) per-module; C) cached projection","A - the platform role directory already exists and is the natural owner.","@Role mentions remain BLOCKED until reverse role-membership lookup exists.","R2","Owner","R2 entry","BLOCKED - pending implementation"),
