 X("D-09","Reporting","PDF runtime owner","PlaywrightPdfReportRenderer exists in code; no runtime is provisioned.","A) Playwright in-host; B) sidecar service; C) third-party service","B - a sidecar keeps a browser runtime out of the web host.","Gates PDF export. Not required for the R4 pilot, which ships HTML, CSV and Excel.","R4+","Owner","Post-R4","OPEN"),
 X("D-10","Reporting","Email delivery integration","ReportDelivery has no transport.","A) reuse Communication channels; B) direct SMTP; C) provider API","A - one delivery path for the product, not two.","Gates scheduled delivery. Depends on Communication activation.","R4+","Owner","Post-R4","OPEN"),
 X("D-11","Reporting","Hosted scheduler ownership","ReportScheduleService has no hosted worker.","A) a new dedicated hosted worker; B) extend the dispatch worker; C) external scheduler","A - a distinct worker with its own scope, matching the platform rule that a hosted service takes IServiceScopeFactory and scopes per run.","Gates scheduling. Not required for the R4 pilot.","R4+","Owner","Post-R4","OPEN"),
 X("D-16","Reporting","SQL vocabulary CHECK constraints","Reporting vocabulary is not constrained in SQL.","A) add CHECK constraints; B) enforce in code only; C) both","B - a second copy of a vocabulary drifts, and it drifts in the dangerous direction. This is why the 15 Never-bootstrap-open actions were deliberately NOT duplicated as a CHECK constraint.","Schema hardening.","R4","Owner","R4 entry","OPEN"),
 X("D-17","Reporting","Report Studio sequence","Whether authoring precedes or follows consumption.","A) Report Center first; B) Studio first; C) together","A - consumption before authoring. R4 delivers the Center; Studio follows.","Sequencing only.","R4","Owner","R4 entry","OPEN"),
